## Drum and dance classes FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="Do I need any experience to join?" %}
Not at all, because both of our classes welcome complete beginners. In fact, our teachers break everything down step by step, so you’ll be drumming or dancing in no time.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How does the $50 first-timer pass work?" %}
If you’ve never been to a class with us, you can grab our Come and Play pass for $50. In short, it covers 4 classes over 4 consecutive weeks, starting from your first class. The pass works for drumming or Afro Dance Fitness. However, it’s non-refundable and non-transferable.
{% /question %}

{% question title="What passes can I buy after that?" %}
After your first 4 classes, a 4-class pass is $80 and a casual class is $25. If you drum and dance, 8-class passes are available too.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Where are the classes held?" %}
All classes run at Palmwoods Memorial Hall, 1 Main St, Palmwoods, so it’s an easy drive for people living across the Sunshine Coast, Noosa and Moreton Bay.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Can I do both classes on the same night?" %}
Yes! Drumming starts at 5.30pm and Afro Dance Fitness follows at 6.30pm. So you can drum first and then dance. In any case, get in touch and we’ll help you choose the best pass.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
{% /section %}

{% section tone="red" %}
